course: dictionary
lesson: 8916
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Side is a good example. In «A square has 4 sides», side means one of the straight lines of the shape. In «move to the side towards space», side means the left or right part of a place.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a shape, a road, a game, or food? Then try your meaning in the sentence. «Whose side are you on?» is about support or teams, not about a shape, so the shape meaning would make no sense there.
explain: Look at the clues in «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side, smashed beyond repair.» The cart is lying down, so side means a surface of the cart, not a straight edge on a shape. The word around it tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Some meanings are casual. «A job on the side» means an extra job, and «no side to her» means she is not stuck-up. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A side is one of the straight lines that make a flat shape, like the 4 sides of a square.
fact: A side can also mean the left or right part of something, or its edge: «the side of the road».
fact: «Side by side» means next to each other, and «take sides» means to support one person or team.
fact: A side can be a team or group in a game or argument, as in «the home side».
fact: «Side effect» means an unwanted result, often of a medicine.
exercise: In «A square has 4 sides», what does side mean? | Extra food served with a meal | *One of the straight lines that make a flat shape | A team in a game | Showing off
exercise: Nadia says, «Whose side are you on?» What does side mean here? | A flat face of a solid | Extra food served with a meal | The left part of a road | *A team or person you support
exercise: «He cooked a side of chips.» What does side mean here? | *Extra food served with a meal | A flat face of a solid | A team in a game | The edge of a road
test: «The shark swung its head from side to side.» What does side mean here? | *Left and right | A straight line on a shape | A team in a game
test: What does «side effect» mean? | A flat shape with 4 sides | *An unwanted result, often of a medicine | A team that wins the game
exam: In a formal essay, «each side gives a bit» could be rewritten with a stiffer word for side. Which word fits? | Lap | Sweet | Shade | *Party
